  "scoreRationale": {
    "shapeVolume": "Rounded hands, sleeves, face edges and compact shoes improve on the faceted source, and torso construction is clearer. The dominating hair mass remains a tall rectangular cap with low straight sides and shallow embedded bumps, impairing the coherent short hairstyle and profile eyewear.",
    "color": "Ellis golden skin, blue-black hair, black spectacles, blue shirt and navy garments remain recognizable. Palette remains warm and readable at logical and phone scale.",
    "lightingHighlights": "Broad balanced overhead/cardinal light gives substantially gentler shading, visible hair/skin/cloth volume and stable all-facing exposure. No directional ground shadow or privileged-facing key was found.",
    "materialDetail": "Native placket/buttons, collar, cuffs, round hands and toe/sole treatment add useful construction. Hair still reads as a soft shell with applied oval bumps and ghost-like smaller fringe forms rather than deliberately organized locks.",
    "artifactFreeReadability": "All576frames and48clips are stable; no new registration, limb attachment, alpha-edge, canvas, atlas-order or clip-loop defect found. The side hairstyle masks almost all useful spectacle/temple shape and weakens identity there, so material visual issues remain."
  },
  "observations": [
    "Compared actual original snapshot, frozen target, independently rendered original source, all576 sealed native frames through48 pixel-verified logical-size sheets, all48 atlases, all59 submitted previews and actual desktop/phone playback. Native main/runtime projects were independently reopened without saving.",
    "The front face, hands and shirt are visibly softer and better constructed than source: rounded palms/thumbs, full sleeves, formed cuffs, collar/placket/buttons and readable compact toe/sole shapes. This is real native geometry/material/light improvement, not a paint-over.",
    "The hair is the outstanding shape failure. In S, the large top ovals sit above a dim row of small rounded lumps embedded in a single dark lower shell. In E/W, the same shell ends in a long nearly straight line through the temple/spectacle level, hiding the useful eyewear profile and leaving a small button-like ear below it. N remains a broad rectangular lower hair wall with scattered oval bumps. This persists in standing, movement, gestures and seated meal frames and is obvious at logical and phone size.",
    "Lighting, skin and cloth shading move toward the selected warm soft style without copying its directional orange rim. The actual active native compositor is a uniform clamped sRGB gain1.35/offset-.175 inside the Blender compositor, with straight/premultiplied alpha conversion; it is present in both modes and is not a per-facing grade.",
    "The held food is explicitly exact canonical packed2D. The alpha128 semantic mapping, canonical fullUV/aspect, actual occupied plate width and bottom-rim pixel-center support are retained. The source0.6 camera-ray depth and all source food-root, yaw and visibility paths are unchanged; empty waiting remains empty.",
    "Food alpha/shadow flags are one static global material/render refinement: BLENDED, no transparency overlap, visible_shadowFalse and transparent_shadowFalse. Matched original-DITHERED/final captures in every food facing/state were inspected; final temporal clips show no material new alpha defect. Source behavior remains archived.",
    "The active import adapter truthfully records compositorTrue and scale2. Its576 measured phase records agree with bound native audits and renders. All2508 original delivery resource path/hash records remain present in the2524-resource adapter. Historical failed hand-weight drafts are preserved and hash-bound; they were not used to infer final attachment quality."
  ],
